this is the most important concept in full stack

Client  →  Server  →  Database
            ↑
            ↓
        Response



- client: it is the application used by the user
- ex: chrome, react app, mobile app etc
- it send request to the server




# server:
- it receives the request, processess them and sends responses back to the client
- ex: nodejs, python,express, spring boot
- it contain business logic: means it does the actual work
- it is the middle man between client and database


#database: stores application data permanently
- ex: mongodb, mysql, postgresql, oracle etc
- it is the permanent storage of the data


